dit/083: ggml-opencl's Adreno xmem attention, made right for Z-Image (stripes and noise on the GPU; Klein was right).
- The cause (found 2026-10-31 with dit/084's per-call switches on Z-Image 512^2): calls whose query rows are not whole
  work-groups. The QK and PV gemms load K and V with sub-group collectives (qcom_sub_group_constant_load8 + sync), and
  the rows past q_width return before them. Z-Image's 1,056 tokens (and the 32-row tail of a 1,024-row split) hit it;
  xmem on its 1,024-row calls only gave the right picture. Such calls now take the generic kernel.
- fp32 where fp16 lost Z-Image's sharp attention (nm-fa-check, dit/082: 10% error at large logits, now under 1%): Q
  is converted unscaled (sd.cpp's kv_scale 1/128 makes the softmax scale ~11, and Q times it overflowed fp16), the QK
  sums are fp32 with the scale applied on store, the score and probability buffers and images and the softmax stats
  are fp32; the PV gemm still reads the probabilities as half ([0, 1]).
Applies after 080 and 081.

